course: dictionary
lesson: 5159
title: Irresponsible and the prefix ir-
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Irresponsible is made of two parts: the prefix ir- and the word responsible. The prefix ir- means not, so irresponsible means not responsible. When you know one part, you can often work out the whole word.
explain: Responsible means someone you can trust to think ahead and look after things. Irresponsible means not thinking about what your actions will cause, or not taking care of things you should look after.
explain: Check your meaning in the sentence: «It was irresponsible of you to leave the gate open.» Leaving the gate open without thinking about what could happen is careless, so irresponsible means careless about results. Swap in your meaning and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Irresponsible means not thinking about the results of what you do, or not taking care of things you should look after.
fact: An irresponsible action is careless and may put people or things in danger.
fact: Common phrases include «irresponsible behaviour», «totally irresponsible» and «it was irresponsible of you to».
fact: The adverb is irresponsibly, as in «He acted irresponsibly», which means he behaved in a careless way.
fact: The prefix ir- means not and goes before words beginning with r, such as irregular and irresponsible. Both words have a double r.
exercise: «Leaving a toddler near the swimming pool was irresponsible.» What does irresponsible mean here? | Happy and playful | Quiet and calm | *Careless, and a danger to the toddler | Very kind and helpful
exercise: Which word is the adverb of irresponsible? | responsibly | irresponsible | *irresponsibly | responsibility
exercise: What does the prefix ir- mean in irresponsible? | Before | Very | *Not | Again
test: Sharing your password with others is irresponsible. What does a safety lesson mean by this? | Funny | Polite | Sensible and careful | *Risky, because it may put your account in danger
test: Which phrase describes someone behaving badly with no thought for the results? | a happy holiday | *irresponsible behaviour | a quiet morning | I was very kind
exam: Which word is formed the same way as irresponsible, with ir- before r? | impossible | unhappy | *irregular | invisible
